▶ ASAMA_04: replay proof, V2 token ve attempt fencing
  ✔ V2 tokens are stable for the stored nonce and change after tombstone GC (23.8114ms)
  ✔ only the same owner, proof and payload can recover a ready reservation (2.5663ms)
  ✔ legacy requestId-only records never regenerate a manage token (0.5526ms)
  ✔ a failed operation retries as a new fenced attempt while preserving its logical tokens (2.1241ms)
  ✔ expired lease takeover fences late finalize and revoke cannot be undone (2.7198ms)
  ✔ 20 simultaneous replays create one logical reservation without UNIQUE failures (3.164ms)
  ✔ isolated PostgreSQL retries the same request id and keeps one row (1711.2588ms)
  ✔ status GET requires cookie and proof, returns ready tokens without any form fields and is no-store (18.6694ms)
